From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: scmi-perf: defer fwnode provider + widen ACPI
 lookup (forward-port of 7.2 0078+0088 for mali_kbase probe)

mali_kbase never binds on 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next: CIXH5000:00 spins in
-EPROBE_DEFER forever ("perf power-domain device not bound yet,
deferring probe", confirmed non-transient via
/sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred). The generic SCMI perf-domain
driver is byte-identical between the 7.0.12 base (SRCREV
f53879e2e1e2fa053040e734c1ef8f386109a61b) and the 7.2 base -- this
kernel's own downstream patch series simply never picked up the two
probe-ordering hardening patches the 7.2 series carries for this exact
file, proven on real hardware there:

  * 0078-pmdomain-fix-dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name-for-sky1-m.patch
    widens scmi_perf_find_proto_fwnode() to first check whether the
    SCMI perf protocol device's OWN fwnode already matches
    sdev->protocol_id (some ACPI layouts describe the "perf"/DVFS
    protocol node directly rather than as an addressable child of a
    separate parent SCMI controller node, which is all the original
    child-walk logic accounted for), with a corrected parent lookup
    (ACPI_COMPANION() then fwnode fallback) for the remaining
    child-walk case. Only the scmi_perf_domain.c hunk of 0078 is
    forward-ported here; its drivers/base/power/common.c and
    drivers/pmdomain/core.c hunks address a distinct
    dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name() EEXIST path not implicated in this
    symptom and are deliberately left out unless real evidence on this
    kernel says otherwise.

  * 0088-pmdomain-scmi-perf-defer-fwnode-provider.patch defers the
    genpd_add_fwnode_provider_onecell() call from
    scmi_perf_domain_probe() itself to late_initcall, once the SCMI
    mailbox/clock tree has settled, instead of registering (or, on
    this kernel, potentially never succeeding at registering) the
    fwnode provider synchronously during probe.

Both are ported together, matching the exact pairing already validated
on 7.2 hardware -- the investigation that root-caused this flagged
these two as likely interdependent. DT boot is unchanged in both
hunks.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c
index 0391d4a..2e36cdb 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c
@@ -109,18 +109,60 @@ static int match_proto_reg(struct acpi_device *adev, void *data)
  *
  * Returns the protocol fwnode, or NULL if not found.
  */
+
+/* Deferred fwnode provider registration - avoids premature consumer
+ * attachment during SCMI protocol bring-up (can SError on unready
+ * hardware under ACPI). Probe stores; late_initcall commits.
+ *
+ * NCZ 2027 (forward-ported from the linux-cix-sky1-ncz 7.2 patch series,
+ * 0088-pmdomain-scmi-perf-defer-fwnode-provider + the scmi_perf_domain.c
+ * hunk of 0078-pmdomain-fix-dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name-for-sky1-mali):
+ * on 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next, mali_kbase's CIXH5000:00 "perf" power-domain
+ * consumer never completes attach and spins in -EPROBE_DEFER forever
+ * (visible in /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred). The 7.2 kernel hit the
+ * same class of bug and fixed it with this exact pairing, proven on real
+ * hardware: (a) widen the ACPI protocol-fwnode lookup below to also match
+ * directly on the SCMI perf protocol device's own fwnode (some ACPI
+ * layouts describe the "perf"/DVFS protocol node without a separate
+ * addressable parent-vs-child split the original child-walk assumed), and
+ * (b) defer the actual genpd_add_fwnode_provider_onecell() call to
+ * late_initcall so it runs after the SCMI mailbox/clock tree has settled.
+ */
+static struct {
+	struct scmi_device *sdev;
+	struct genpd_onecell_data *pd_data;
+	struct fwnode_handle *proto_fw;
+} scmi_perf_deferred;
+
 static struct fwnode_handle *scmi_perf_find_proto_fwnode(struct scmi_device *sdev)
 {
 	struct acpi_device *parent_adev;
+	struct fwnode_handle *fw = dev_fwnode(&sdev->dev);
 	struct proto_fwnode_match match = {
 		.protocol_id = sdev->protocol_id,
 		.result = NULL,
 	};
+	u32 reg;
 
 	if (sdev->dev.of_node)
 		return NULL;
 
-	parent_adev = to_acpi_device_node(dev_fwnode(&sdev->dev));
+	/*
+	 * Under ACPI the SCMI perf protocol device may be created directly
+	 * on the protocol child node (e.g. \_SB.SCMI.DVFS with reg matching
+	 * the protocol id). Consumers reference that same node in
+	 * power-domains; the provider must be registered on its own fwnode
+	 * in that case rather than on a sibling search rooted at what would
+	 * otherwise be treated as the parent SCMI controller node.
+	 */
+	if (fw && !fwnode_property_read_u32(fw, "reg", &reg) &&
+	    reg == sdev->protocol_id)
+		return fw;
+
+	/* Fallback: walk SCMI controller children (legacy / usual layout). */
+	parent_adev = ACPI_COMPANION(sdev->dev.parent);
+	if (!parent_adev)
+		parent_adev = to_acpi_device_node(dev_fwnode(sdev->dev.parent));
 	if (!parent_adev)
 		return NULL;
 
@@ -215,10 +257,10 @@ static int scmi_perf_domain_probe(struct scmi_device *sdev)
 
 		proto_fw = scmi_perf_find_proto_fwnode(sdev);
 		if (proto_fw) {
-			ret = genpd_add_fwnode_provider_onecell(proto_fw,
-								scmi_pd_data);
-			if (ret)
-				goto err;
+			scmi_perf_deferred.sdev = sdev;
+			scmi_perf_deferred.pd_data = scmi_pd_data;
+			scmi_perf_deferred.proto_fw = proto_fw;
+			dev_info(dev, "%s: fwnode provider deferred to late_initcall\n", __func__);
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -320,6 +362,23 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(scmi_perf_domain_power_scale);
 
 module_scmi_driver(scmi_perf_domain_driver);
 
+static int __init scmi_perf_deferred_init(void)
+{
+	if (scmi_perf_deferred.sdev && scmi_perf_deferred.pd_data &&
+	    scmi_perf_deferred.proto_fw) {
+		int ret = genpd_add_fwnode_provider_onecell(
+			scmi_perf_deferred.proto_fw,
+			scmi_perf_deferred.pd_data);
+		if (ret)
+			pr_err("scmi_perf: late fwnode provider failed: %d\n", ret);
+		else
+			pr_info("scmi_perf: late fwnode provider registered (%d domains)\n",
+				scmi_perf_deferred.pd_data->num_domains);
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+late_initcall(scmi_perf_deferred_init);
+
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Ulf Hansson <ulf.hansson@linaro.org>");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("ARM SCMI perf domain driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2");
--
2.51.0
